Good call — a separate consumer group per topic gives you **independent offsets, independent rebalances, and fault isolation** (a lagging or failing topic never affects the others). The only architectural change is: instead of one `KafkaReceiver` subscribed to all topics, the pipeline spins up **one `KafkaReceiver` per handler**, each with its own `group.id`.

Here's the updated design.

---

## 1. Extend the SPI with per-topic consumer settings

```java
public interface TopicHandler<T> {

    String topic();
    Class<T> payloadType();
    String extractNationalCode(T payload);
    Mono<Void> onMatch(T payload, String nationalCode);
    default Mono<Void> onNoMatch(T payload, String nationalCode) { return Mono.empty(); }

    /** Consumer group for this topic. Default: derived from topic name; can be overridden in YAML. */
    default String consumerGroup() {
        return "ncc-" + topic().replace('.', '-');
    }

    /** Optional Kafka consumer property overrides for this topic only (e.g. auto.offset.reset). */
    default Map<String, Object> consumerOverrides() {
        return Map.of();
    }
}
```

Handlers can set it explicitly:

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class LoanRequestHandler implements TopicHandler<LoanRequestEvent> {
    private final ResilientApiClient api;

    @Override public String topic()          { return "loan.requests"; }
    @Override public String consumerGroup()  { return "loan-national-code-checker"; }
    @Override public Map<String, Object> consumerOverrides() {
        return Map.of(ConsumerConfig.AUTO_OFFSET_RESET_CONFIG, "earliest",
                      ConsumerConfig.MAX_POLL_RECORDS_CONFIG, 200);
    }
    // ... rest unchanged
}
```

