## 2. Make it overridable from configuration (ops-friendly)

So group IDs / concurrency can be changed per environment without a code change:

```java
@ConfigurationProperties("app")
@Validated
public record AppProperties(
        Kafka kafka,
        Map<String, ConsumerSettings> consumers,   // keyed by topic name
        Redis redis, Api api, Processing processing) {

    public record Kafka(@Min(1) int defaultPartitionConcurrency) {}

    public record ConsumerSettings(
            String groupId,                       // null -> use handler default
            Integer partitionConcurrency,         // null -> app.kafka.default-partition-concurrency
            Boolean enabled,                      // null -> true; allows disabling one topic
            Map<String, String> properties) {     // raw kafka consumer overrides
        public boolean isEnabled() { return enabled == null || enabled; }
    }

    public ConsumerSettings consumerFor(String topic) {
        return consumers == null ? null : consumers.get(topic);
    }
    public record Redis(@NotBlank String keyPrefix, Duration timeout) {}
    public record Api(@NotBlank String baseUrl, Duration timeout) {}
    public record Processing(Duration timeout) {}
}
```

```yaml
spring:
  kafka:
    bootstrap-servers: localhost:9092
    consumer:
      # NOTE: no group-id here anymore – it's per topic
      auto-offset-reset: earliest
      max-poll-records: 500

app:
  kafka.default-partition-concurrency: 16
  consumers:
    loan.requests:
      group-id: loan-ncc-prod
      partition-concurrency: 32
    card.issued:
      group-id: card-ncc-prod
      properties:
        max.poll.records: "100"
    kyc.updates:
      enabled: false          # pause a whole business without redeploying
```

Resolution order: **YAML override → handler `consumerGroup()` → derived default**.

